ADR-090: the informe moves down to Xangarro, the pricing cards say the real numbers, and the PAC must survive reuse

informeMensual is true on both paid tiers — Xangarro already rendered the LLM
conclusiones, so gating the cheaper deterministic PDF higher was backwards,
and the contador PDF is the retention hook where retention is won. Pricing
copy follows the table C-12 landed (300/50, 10k/1k + informe, 30k/5k; no more
"ilimitado" lines). The mock gains the over-limit scenario (C-12 step 6) and
the informe e2e's negative case moves to a free-plan tenant. The PAC chosen
for subscription CFDIs must be API-first and multi-emisor: the same wiring is
the foundation for a future tenant-facing facturación add-on; per-tenant CSD
onboarding is that add-on's real cost.
